      <!-- Project Timeline -->
      <div class="sp-db-section sp-fade-in">
        <div class="sp-db-section-label">The Process</div>
        <h3>Project Timeline</h3>
        <p>Design and installation projects take time and communication. This timeline highlights each stage of the process and the approximate timing you would expect. Communication is key and we will work together to meet the needs of you and your clients.</p>
        <img class="sp-db-timeline-img sp-fade-in" src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0652/8044/2581/files/project_timeline_2.png?v=1772328991" alt="Project Timeline">
      </div>

      <!-- Our Design Process -->
      <div class="sp-db-section sp-fade-in">
        <div class="sp-db-section-label">How We Work</div>
        <h3>Our Design Process</h3>
        <p>Our design process begins with a sales visit where we discuss your requirements and vision for the space. Following this, our team creates a comprehensive design proposal and quotation tailored to your needs.</p>
        <p>Once you decide to proceed, you raise a Purchase Order and arrange a 50% deposit. We then conduct a thorough site survey to ensure all custom items are made to measure. Your signed proposal places the order, and installation takes place 8-10 weeks from that point.</p>
        <div class="sp-db-two-col sp-fade-in">
          <div>
            <h4>Design Visuals</h4>
            <p>We supply multiple site visuals of the proposed design, giving you a clear picture of how your finished space will look. These detailed renders show the room from various angles, helping you visualise the placement of every element.</p>
            <img class="sp-db-zoom-img sp-fade-in" src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0652/8044/2581/files/stand_alone_design.png?v=1772229413" alt="Design Visual Example" data-zoomable>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4>Design Plan</h4>
            <p>Each proposal includes a design plan showing your layout in plan form. All products are numbered on the plan and listed alongside, providing a comprehensive overview of the equipment placement and room configuration.</p>
            <img class="sp-db-zoom-img sp-fade-in" src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0652/8044/2581/files/plan.png?v=1772230042" alt="Design Plan Example" data-zoomable>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Site Survey -->
      <div class="sp-db-section sp-fade-in">
        <div class="sp-db-section-label">Preparation</div>
        <h3>Booking the Site Survey</h3>
        <p>The speed at which a room is completed is dependent upon the readiness of the room. A site survey will be undertaken as soon as possible, but only when Mike Ayres Design have been informed the room is in its finished state, including:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Electrical work (if required)</li>
          <li>All building work or alterations complete (including ceilings &amp; 2nd fix items)</li>
          <li>Any hoists or lifting equipment is in situ</li>
          <li>All fixtures and fittings complete, including air conditioning or heating units</li>
          <li>Clean and empty, free from all obstructions</li>
          <li>Unoccupied and available for our staff to have minimum 1 hour uninterrupted access</li>
        </ul>
        <p>It is always advisable that you view our installation services as the final stage of your building/room preparation process. Once we come to install, your environment will be cleaned and ready to use straight away.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Project Brief -->
      <div class="sp-db-section sp-fade-in">
        <div class="sp-db-section-label">Your Vision</div>
        <h3>The Project Brief</h3>
        <p>Every project starts with your brief. You tell us about your new space, and we outline your requirements along with additional design notes and considerations.</p>
        <p>Our design team considers every aspect of the environment &mdash; from suspension points for swings, to wall and floor matting for safety, climbing equipment for gross motor development, and flexible items that allow therapists to create sensory circuits around the room.</p>
        <div class="sp-db-two-col sp-fade-in">
          <div>
            <h4>Product Descriptions</h4>
            <p>Each design proposal includes detailed descriptions of the key items seen within the design. From rocking barrels and platform swings to climbing walls and sensory loungers, we ensure you understand the purpose and therapeutic benefit of every piece of equipment.</p>
            <img class="sp-db-zoom-img sp-fade-in" src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0652/8044/2581/files/Screenshot_2026-02-27_231708.png?v=1772234245" alt="Product Descriptions Example" data-zoomable>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4>Colour Choices</h4>
            <p>We provide a comprehensive selection of colour choices for the various made-to-order items in your design. From PU fabrics for bean chairs, vinyl for wall cushions and floor mats, to soft textured fabrics for sensory rockers &mdash; your space is customised to your preference.</p>
            <img class="sp-db-zoom-img sp-fade-in" src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0652/8044/2581/files/Screenshot_2026-03-11_173359.png?v=1773268245" alt="Colour Choices Example" data-zoomable>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

